markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Loops: Automating Repetitive Tasks</h1>
<img src="https://images.code.org/5c6d14afb3172265d27dae69924fd194-image-1741621155625.png" alt="Icon of arrows making a circle symbolizing a loop" width="105px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0 20px 10px 0;">
<p>Imagine painting the same white square five times in a row, one line of code for each one.</p>
<p>Instead of writing that same instruction over and over, a loop lets you write it once and repeat it automatically.</p>
<div style="clear:both;"></div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>📖 Loop:</b> A structure that repeats a set of instructions multiple times, so you do not have to write the same code over and over.</p>
</div>


<h2>While Loops: Repeat Until a Condition is Met</h2>
<p>A <code style="font-size:14px;">while</code> loop is perfect for this task because it keeps running until a condition is no longer true.</p>
<p>This is like saying:</p>
<p style="font-style: italic;">"Keep painting until there is no white space left."</p>
<p>By using a loop, you don't have to write the same instruction five separate times, you just repeat the action until the job is done!</p>

<p>Let's walk through how this actually gets written in code.</p>






---

